From: EglantinePS5
Subject: up: EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_PREPASS: the shader set is prepared before the game starts (list keys first, every worker, full duty, no cap, resumable), off by default

Why: test d4 (13 Nov 2026, run1366) showed the whole-game shader set holds the keys the game asks
for (43 of 43 sorted by EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY: 28 served, 15 in the set but not prepared yet, 0 near,
0 without a record; the Mac key check found 441 of d4's 458 first_start.list graphics keys in the
set). What failed was time: beside the game at 1 job, 50% duty and a 5,000 cap, 820 of 113,054
records were prepared (185 ms a record) before the 384 MB memory floor stopped it at 500 s.

What, with EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_PREPASS=1 (needs EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET=1, EDEN_UP_CANONICAL_KEYS=1 and the
prepared store, as the set itself): in LoadDiskResources, after the boot's own pipelines and
PrepareKept and before StartShaderSet (so before system.Run(): the game's memory is not taken yet),
on the loading thread:
1. the set file is made or reused (ShaderSet::Prepare; a first conversion runs at full duty through
   the new ShaderSet::OverrideDuty and is not cut by the time limit). StartShaderSet's thread then
   uses this result instead of preparing it again.
2. one key-only read of the file counts what is left: every usable key not in the kept store, each
   once (the set has about 73,400 distinct keys in 113,054 records; a repeated key is now queued
   once, also with several jobs in flight).
3. list keys: G rows of first_start.list / first_start.prev.list (header must name this cache
   version, driver, lowering tag and canonical=1) and graphics records of EGPLIST1 pipeline lists
   (0720 format; key taken with this driver's fields) found as *.list in the shader folder and the
   title folder, plus EDEN_UP_PIPELINE_LIST_IMPORT=<path> when it names a file.
4. PrepareShaderSet runs with a ShaderSetPass: first over the listed keys, then over the records of
   programs earlier sessions saw live (prep_shader_set.live), then the rest of the file. No cap,
   full duty, on threads of its own: EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_PREPASS_WORKERS=<n> (default one per core
   but one, at most 16), made for the prepass and gone after it, so EDEN_NX2_PIPELINE_WORKERS (2 in
   d4) keeps its meaning for play. Each job is the existing one: translate, driver build with the
   driver's own cache only (prep_no_cache), keep SPIR-V/infos/answers, drop the pipeline.
It ends when all is done; at EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_PREPASS_MAX_S=<s> counted from the prepass start;
under the disk floor (EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_MIN_FREE_DISK_MB, checked every 64 queued as before); after
EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_PREPASS_MEMORY_WAIT_S (300) under the memory floor (it waits, polling every 250 ms,
while jobs in flight give memory back; the background pass stops at once instead); or when a file
shader_set_prepass.skip appears in the shader or title folder (checked every second, removed, so it
skips one start). What is left goes on beside the game as before (StartShaderSet: live first, then
the file up to EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_MAX unless EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_PREP_ALL=1) and at the next start.
Resumable: a key in the kept store is never queued again; the index is committed at most once a
minute and at the end, so a kill loses at most a minute of work. A pass that reads the whole file
writes the existing "every record is known" marker, so later starts skip the read.

Shown: the boot screen counts the set's records (LoadCallbackStage::Prepare, which the core never
sent before; the headless front adds records a second and minutes left: front commit, same T157
commit). Log: a start line, one line with the counts (keys left, known, repeats, list files, disk
needed vs free), a progress line every 10 s (done/total, listed done, rate, minutes left, kept,
failed, free memory, free disk, store size) and an end line with totals and why it ended.
Disk: if std::filesystem::space() cannot be read the floor check now says so once (it was silent).

Off: one cached switch read in LoadDiskResources; PrepareShaderSet takes a null pass (each new
branch tests it); DutyPercent reads one relaxed atomic. Nothing else changes.

Cost estimate (our notes in the T157 folder): about 73,400 builds for a full set, about 1.5 GiB of
kept store (21 KiB a record, d4), the driver's disk cache about 0.5 GiB more (estimate). At d4's 185
ms a record per worker: 73,400 x 0.185 s / 8 workers = about 28 min; at the 7-8 ms a record the
own-record preparation shows on 8 workers before play (about 60 ms per worker): about 9 min. Not
measured on the console.

Test: EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_PREPASS=1 with the set's usual switches; look for "Shader set prepass"
lines (rate, minutes left, end line), the boot screen's count, and in play EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY
totals with exact_not_prepared near 0. A second start should say "known already" for what the
first did and finish fast.

Credits: the shader set (0501, 0522, 0528, 0529; our v3.1 draft, Fritchii's recipe and
extractor), the first-start list (0595), the pipeline list format (0720).
